RDG → SID → MFE → PED 
=====================================================================
RDG (Relational Directed Geometry): Objects and directed relations G = (Obj, 
Rel). Morphisms preserve existing arrows without adding new ones; sub-RDGs 
are component-wise inclusions.

SID (Structure–Interaction–Dynamics): Layers a geometry as S(G) ⊆ I(G) ⊆ D(G) 
⊆ G, where S is the invariant skeleton, I the operational links, and D the 
completed dynamical paths.

MFE (Momentum–Flux Engine): A bipolar dynamical system on states E(t) = (M, F, 
M̄, F̄) with update map Φ, living in a domain D_MFE ⊆ ℝ⁴. It maintains bounded 
oscillation via the pairs (M, M̄) and (F, F̄) with no runaway or dead-stall.

PED (Power–Evaluation–Dynamic-slice): Extracts power P(E) = ½(M² + F²), an 
evaluation functional V, and the next dynamic slice Φ(E).

